%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against ARCHITECTURE.md S12 + D33 as amended by D45 + D27
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Customer
    participant SYS as ReadyCall
    participant AI as Analysis
    participant A as Agent
    participant OTHER as The agent's OTHER systems
    participant STORE as readycall store

    C->>SYS: hangs up
    SYS->>SYS: IN_CALL to WRAP_UP (the CALL record)
    SYS->>SYS: agent -> AFTER_CALL_WORK (presence)
    Note over SYS,A: ACW is a REAL STATE, not a gap (D33).<br/>No new call is offered during it.

    par the customer is asked to rate
        SYS->>C: "ให้คะแนน 1 ถึง 5"
        C->>SYS: presses 4
    and the agent gets a head start
        SYS->>AI: summarise the whole call
        AI-->>A: PRE-FILLED summary + suggested disposition
        Note right of AI: pre-filled, never auto-saved.<br/>The agent owns the record.
    end

    A->>A: edits the summary
    A->>SYS: disposition + follow-ups, then SAVE
    SYS->>STORE: call record closed
    SYS->>SYS: WRAP_UP to RATING to CLOSED
    Note over SYS,STORE: saving finishes OUR work. It does NOT<br/>mean the agent is free. (D45)

    opt the work that is not in our system
        A->>OTHER: updates another internal tool
        A->>OTHER: writes a note, asks a colleague, files a form
    end

    A->>SYS: clicks READY
    SYS->>SYS: AFTER_CALL_WORK to AVAILABLE
    Note right of SYS: ONLY the person ends ACW. The timer may<br/>auto-save the record so a call cannot hang<br/>open - it must NEVER auto-ready. (D45)

    Note over A,SYS: common case is still one click:<br/>the workstation offers "Save & Ready" together.

    Note over STORE: BOTH sides rate (D27). The agent rates the call<br/>too, which is how we learn whether the brief<br/>was actually any good.
